  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Stack Light",
    "description": "A squat white-and-orange lighthouse high on a sea stack, joined to a clifftop on the shore by a rope bridge with nothing under it but the sea. A lighthouse this high needs no tall tower: the stack lifts its lantern for it. The lantern and window light up after dark in World View. 29 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Sea Stack** — four dark Block 2x2s, two side by side and two more on top, make a stack 4 by 2 and four high, standing out of the water, with Rocks round its foot.\n2. **Cliff** — two grey Block 2x2s stacked on the shore make the clifftop, as high as the stack. A Ladder, turned 90° (press **R**), climbs its landward face from a Rock on the beach.\n3. **Rope Bridge** — two wooden Plate 2x4s, turned 90°, cross from the cliff to the stack with no pier. A Post stands at each corner of the bridge, and four Logs run between them for the ropes, two along each side.\n4. **Tower** — one white Block 2x2 on the seaward half of the stack, so the bridge lands on open stone. The orange Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; a Small Window looks out to sea and glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — an orange Round Plate 2x2, a Lantern that lights up after dark, another orange Round Plate 2x2 and an orange Cone Roof.\n\nStand the cliff at the water's edge and the stack out in the water: the rope bridge is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Sea Stack: 4 Block 2x2, 4 Rock\n- Cliff: 2 Block 2x2, 1 Rock, 1 Ladder\n- Rope Bridge: 2 Plate 2x4, 4 Post, 4 Log\n- Tower: 1 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n29 bricks in all.\n",
